  "output": "The book follows a brass-rank magitech artificer who takes a routine guild job in a ruin that is folded out of space and stuck in a single looping hour [1]. The story involves a party taking a location known as \"the Nine\" and finding it is \"wrong\" [3]. The narrative explores themes of magic being a shattered art tiered into \"Facets,\" some of which are lost or forbidden [4], and a character's journey from hiding their ability to feel these deep Facets to eventually inheriting \"the problem of the Whole\" [5].\n\nThe protagonist is **Cael Ferren** [2, 5]. She is a 26-year-old brass-rank artificer who has spent her life hiding the fact that she can feel the deep, forbidden Facets of magic [2, 5]. While she desires an unremarkable career at the Commission Hall, she must eventually face the truth that the \"hum\" she feels is a compass to a magic the world broke on purpose [5].",
